rom 58.9 million residents on January 1, 2025, the population will drop to 55 million in 2050, the stats agency said.\nIn 2080, however, the number is expected to be 45.8 million: over 13 million fewer than today.\nFurthermore, the number of couples with children is expected to decrease until it falls below those without children: from the current 7.5 million, 28.1% of the total, it will drop to 5.8 million in 2050, when they will represent just 21.1% of families. Childless couples, on the other hand, are increasing: from 5.4 million in 2025 to 5.9 million in 2050 (+8.8%). Their share of the total will rise to 21.4%. (ANSA).Read article...", "published_at": "2026-08-31T11:14:58+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.ansa.it/webimages/img_1280x720/2026/8/31/817a03aaffc45eb093c13376a15f19e9.jpg", "source": {"name": "ANSA (English)", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.ansa.it/english/"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 15, "confidence": 0.292, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 0.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 36.8, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "d09e311f-6d90-4426-b670-8ae8f79987b1", "title": "CBCG: Outflow amounts to €239.97 million - Agencija MINA", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxNU3VYeXR1SXhGS3R2TWtJNG9xVENYS29CSU0xSjV5WXgtUlU0QnNiVWVPbkdVSlk1NkFIQlJSMVNMQm1Yc3BvNUFjckF5dVRMa2RTek1iYmFCaFpia25Lekh5ZGwxMnR2QlhmSFA5UUxDTVN1SFNPcnpWNkw3TDc1bzN3?oc=5", "summary": "CBCG: Outflow amounts to €239.97 millionAgencija MINA", "published_at": "2026-08-30T19:21:09+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "MINA (Montenegro News Agency)", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://mina.news/en"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 6, "confidence": 0.15, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 0.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 0.0, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "f554e900-e602-4836-9a27-82a157461652", "title": "Over 13 million fewer residents in Italy in 2080", "url": "https://www.ansa.it/english/news/2026/08/31/over-13-million-fewer-residents-in-italy-in-2080_61abf83a-2622-4c0f-a52f-b3e8d351540c.html", "summary": "(ANSA) - ROME, AUG 31 - Italy's population will continue to decline and age and it will have over 13 million fewer residents by 2080, Istat said Monday.\nFrom 58.9 million residents on January 1, 2025, the population will drop to 55 million in 2050, the stats agency said.\nIn 2080, however, the number is expected to be 45.8 million: over 13 million fewer than today.\nFurthermore, the number of couples with children is expected to decrease until it falls below those without children: from the current 7.5 million, 28.1% of the total, it will drop to 5.8 million in 2050, when they will represent just 21.1% of families. Childless couples, on the other hand, are increasing: from 5.4 million in 2025 to 5.9 million in 2050 (+8.8%). Their share of the total will rise to 21.4%. (ANSA).Read article...", "published_at": "2026-08-31T11:20:16+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.ansa.it/webimages/img_1280x720/2026/8/31/817a03aaffc45eb093c13376a15f19e9.jpg", "source": {"name": "ANSA (English)", "tier": "international", "url": "https://www.ansa.it/english/"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 15, "confidence": 0.292, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 0.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 0.0, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 36.8, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}]